                ]

                comment Cmt_Overview START <p><b>REGFM_A1 droop-controlled grid-forming (GFM) controller</b></p><p>Implements W. Du et al., <i>Model Specification of Droop-Controlled, Grid-Forming Inverters (REGFM_A1)</i>, PNNL-32278 (V6), reproduced from the PNNL PSCAD model.</p><p>The inverter is a voltage source E∠δE behind the coupling reactance XL (Fig. 1-2). This block computes E and δE with P-f and Q-V droop (Fig. 3) and limits the fault current (Fig. 4, Eq. 7).</p><p>Signal flow: abc measurements → αβ → filtered P, Q, V → droop loops → E, θ → Ea/Eb/Ec references → current limiter → voltage sources.</p><p>Rates: droop/PI loops and Pref/Qref/Vref at Ts; measurements, θ, EMF waveforms and the limiter at Ts_mod (default 0.2·Ts).</p><p>All parameters are on the inverter rating base and come from the GFM Inverter mask (Table 1).</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 5860, 6124
                ]

                comment Cmt_Measurements START <p><b>1. Measurements and αβ transform</b></p><p>Va..Vc (phase-neutral) and Ia..Ic (output current) arrive at Ts_mod; rate transitions bring them to Ts.</p><p>Amplitude-invariant Clarke transform (stationary frame, no PLL):<br/>Vds = 2/3·Va − 1/3·(Vb + Vc),&nbsp; Vqs = (Vb − Vc)/√3; Ids, Iqs likewise.</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 5772, 6816
                ]

                comment Cmt_Magnitudes START <p><b>2. Magnitudes:</b> V = √(Vds² + Vqs²)·√3/√2 / Vbase (line-line RMS, pu), filtered by TVf (Eq. 6) → V_pu;&nbsp; |I| = √(Ids² + Iqs²) in pu → I_pu.</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 7456, 6300
                ]

                comment Cmt_PQ START <p><b>3. Power</b></p><p>P = 1.5·(Vds·Ids + Vqs·Iqs)/Sbase<br/>Q = 1.5·(Vqs·Ids − Vds·Iqs)/Sbase</p><p>filtered by TPf and TQf (Eq. 4-5) → Pf_pu, Qf_pu.</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 8400, 7260
                ]

                comment Cmt_QV START <p><b>4. Q-V droop (Fig. 3b):</b> V_ref = Vref − mq·(Qf − Qref) + Q_lim, where the Qmax/Qmin PI loops (kpqmax, kiqmax) act only when Qf leaves Qmin..Qmax.</p><p>VFlag = 1: PI_V (kpv, kiv, output limited to Emin..Emax) regulates the filtered terminal voltage to V_ref → Edroop. VFlag = 0: V_ref is used as Edroop directly.</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 6708, 7512
                ]

                comment Cmt_Pf START <p><b>5. P-f droop (Fig. 3a):</b> ω = 2πf0·(1 + w1 + w2), w1 = mp·(Pref − Pf); w2 comes from the Pmax/Pmin PI loops (kppmax, kipmax), active only when Pf leaves Pmin..Pmax (overload mitigation). f = ω/2π → f_drp.</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 7984, 7532
                ]

                comment Cmt_EMF START <p><b>6. Internal EMF:</b> θ = ∫ω dt (δdroop, wraps at 2π, at Ts_mod). Ea/Eb/Ec references = E·sin(θ), E·sin(θ + 240°), E·sin(θ + 120°) (positive sequence), with E = Edroop, scaled to volts.</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 6752, 8128
                ]

                comment Cmt_Probes START <p><b>Probes:</b> filtered P, Q, V (Pf_pu, Qf_pu, V_PUss), internal frequency f_drp, EMF magnitude E_pu, limit-loop outputs and lim_on.</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 8688, 8128
                ]

                comment Cmt_Params START <p><b>Parameters and bases</b> (GFM Inverter mask, Table 1): Vbase, Sbase, ωbase, current base, P/Q/E limits, VFlag. External set points Pref_in, Qref_in, Vref_in (pu).</p> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 6752, 9272
                ]

                comment Cmt_Limiter START <!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC "-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN" "http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd"><html><head><meta name="qrichtext" content="1" /><meta charset="utf-8" /><style type="text/css">p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }li.unchecked::marker { content: "\2610"; }li.checked::marker { content: "\2612"; }</style></head><body style=" font-family:'Sans'; font-size:12pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;"><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;"><span style=" font-weight:700;">7. Fault current limiter (Fig. 4, Eq. 7)</span>, C function Fig4_Lim at Ts_mod: predicts I = (Edroop − V)/(Rc + jXL) in αβ.</p><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;">If |I| &gt; ImaxF, E = V + (Rc + jXL)·ImaxF∠φ = V + (ImaxF/|I|)·(Edroop − V) (current held at ImaxF, angle kept); otherwise the droop EMF passes through. </p><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;">lim_on = 1 while limiting. </p><p style=" margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;">Ea/Eb/Ec drive the inverter voltage sources.</p></body></html> ENDCOMMENT 
                [
                    position = 7036, 8656
                ]

                connect Fr_Van_1 G_Va_2_3.in as Connection1
                connect Fr_Vbn_2 G_Vb_1_3.in as Connection2
